[38;5;231m⏺[39m One more structural question, then I'll bring you approaches.

  The codebase has two incompatible module worlds: [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is a plain browser script loaded via [38;5;153m<script src="app.js">[39m
  with everything as globals, while [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m use CommonJS [38;5;153mrequire[39m/[38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m and [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m
  declares [38;5;153m"main": "src/index.js"[39m. A session module that "other forms will need later" has to live in one of them, and
  browsers can't [38;5;153mrequire[39m.

  - [1mES modules for the new code[0m — add [38;5;153mtype="module"[39m to the script tag, write [38;5;153msrc/session.js[39m with [38;5;153mexport[39m, import it from
    [38;5;153mapp.js[39m. Modern, works natively in browsers, no build step. Costs: [38;5;153mapp.js[39m becomes a module (deferred execution, no
    more implicit globals), and it sits alongside the existing CommonJS files rather than converting them.
  - [1mBrowser global[0m — [38;5;153msrc/session.js[39m attaches a [38;5;153mSession[39m object to [38;5;153mwindow[39m, loaded by a second [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m.
    Zero disruption to anything that exists. Costs: it's a global, load order matters, and it's not importable from the
    Node side or by tests.
  - [1mConvert the whole project to ESM[0m — [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m, rewrite [38;5;153mutils.js[39m and [38;5;153mindex.js[39m. One consistent
    world. Costs: touches files unrelated to your request.

  I recommend ES modules for the new code only: it's the direction the [38;5;153msrc/[39m tree would go anyway, it makes the session
  module unit-testable, and it leaves [38;5;153mutils.js[39m/[38;5;153mindex.js[39m alone — converting them isn't part of what you asked for.
